{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pulls/30","id":4450091491,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTwsbvM8AAAABCT8B4w","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pull/30","diff_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pull/30.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pull/30.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/issues/30","number":30,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: rework SLICE-V1-003 advertising authority and operating flow","user":{"login":"Corwin-Code","id":219115063,"node_id":"U_kgDODQ9uNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219115063?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The reviewed advertising flow could qualify stale Outcome inputs, lose cause-specific responsibility, and resolve current Outcome Policy without the required scope/conflict state. This R1 rework gives calculation, Preview, Planner and human/manual selection the same exact authority, while preserving proven-harm responsibility and immutable completed-action policy versions.\n\nCurrent published source checkpoint: `02e617278793b4458dfb7cac74c2a937f1dfcb00`, tree `8d8dd0b3429797a0e01b2ff91c1ba5c09de17dcc`. The nine complete verification layers and exact current CI evidence are **in progress**. The 22-Finding and 200-criterion engineering matrices remain pending complete evidence admission. Independent Controller verification remains pending. This PR stays **Draft / Open / Unmerged**.\n\nV0072 resolves applicable Outcome Policy by geographic and cause specificity, refuses incomparable or duplicate maxima, and exposes OUTCOME_POLICY_UNRESOLVED / OUTCOME_POLICY_CONFLICTED without fallback. Current selection also verifies the exact bound Policy; missing authority cannot produce a new frozen baseline. Each manual option retains its own blocker codes. Completed actions continue to use their frozen original Policy and thresholds after a new version or conflict appears.\n\nThe same-class scan found that positive recoverable value required a Bid above Max CPC while an Increase required a Bid below it. The calculator now uses static economic space in the same observed cohort, capped by both Max CPC and original allowable spend, with four-decimal downward rounding, matched currency and preserved evidence grades. Each qualification tier applies its own amount and confidence thresholds. The original Target and Task/write policy limits remain unchanged. New application/PostgreSQL tests derive a real Increase candidate and Maker selection with an attested canonical baseline; missing/conflicted Policy refuses selection without new baseline or execution authority.\n\nThe earlier repairs remain: per-source and per-purpose frozen Freshness; shared cause-bound economic protection; independent physical risk-clear outcomes; immutable revisions; representative mixed Outcome/control-state orchestration; exact platform/store/semantic scope; one-query resolution of all 48 typed Freshness inputs; persisted operational-association inference limits; and UTC/microsecond storage and sealed reentry regressions.\n\nValidation scope so far:\n\n- The pre-checkpoint complete unit diagnostic passed all 1630 nodes. A separate final focused run passed 33 headroom unit nodes and all five Optimization PostgreSQL nodes. They are diagnostic source records, not a combined full-regression total.\n- The latest narrow correction passed all 46 privilege/policy nodes and the complete frontend quality diagnostic, including 337 tests, format/types/coverage and build. The source preparation passed all 421 governance tests; the three generated engineering views remain verification-pending.\n- Unfiltered `clean verify` with original coverage and capacity thresholds is now running on the exact clean checkpoint and complete 1278-file source inventory. All remaining layers will bind that same source.\n- Historical 7e66cf8 completed its full backend run with 2644 passing nodes and successful exact CI. The 1381ef7 local run was stopped after its completed exact-function-list failure (2040 passing nodes, one failure, exit143; no capacity measurement). Its Frontend CI lint failure is separately preserved. The new checkpoint corrects only the missing four read-only helper signatures/ACL assertions and three frontend lint expressions; controls and original refusal checks remain. Earlier failed records stay separate and supply no current-source admission.\n\nControl references remain unchanged: accepted Contract SHA-256 `1606a844934c49a9e67dc0a1a15d49f4003913efc678bae94403c3c29ecb811c`; Frozen Finding Set JSON SHA-256 `f4af74f5086772dc70c3ec3cc7aa8808e9441e96109d301b145e70c18f6131a0`; effective Owner authority `OWNER_CODEX_SLICE_V1_003_ROOT_CAUSE_REWORK_R1`. Original V0001–V0071 bytes and W10 Controller verdict/measurement identities are preserved. Source changes and diagnostic limits are recorded in `docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/rework-r1/final-gate-r1/POST-7e66cf8-OUTCOME-POLICY-REWORK.md` and `POST-1381ef7-VERIFICATION-FIX.md`.\n\n`production_write_enabled=false`. The 24 release obligations retain their production boundary. Publication is append-only on the named branch. Ready, merge, force-push, real Provider access and shared/production operations remain outside this work.\n","created_at":"2026-09-05T10:24:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T03:10:46Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2b3e8e4b60f4d7a22afe1616f205e218d29a178c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pulls/30/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pulls/30/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/issues/30/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/statuses/02e617278793b4458dfb7cac74c2a937f1dfcb00","head":{"label":"Corwin-Code:feat/SLICE-V1-003-advertising-traffic-efficiency","ref":"feat/SLICE-V1-003-advertising-traffic-efficiency","sha":"02e617278793b4458dfb7cac74c2a937f1dfcb00","user":{"login":"Corwin-Code","id":219115063,"node_id":"U_kgDODQ9uNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219115063?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Corwin-Code/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.c